                <pb facs="1569" n="1411" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1411"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Jay to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25,
                        1906</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1370.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In accordance with the department’s
                    instruction No. 1046, of March 15, 1906, I have the honor to inclose a
                    translation from the Turkish text of the special law of 1883 governing the
                    holding of real estate in Turkey by subjects of Ottoman birth who have changed
                    their nationality, and a translation, with explanations, of certain articles of
                    the general Ottoman land code of 1858 which are referred to in the special
                    law.</p>
                <p>I am indebted to Mr. A. K. Schmavonian, the very able and Obliging legal adviser
                    employed by the legation in straightening out the transfer of property of
                    American institutions, for this information and these translations.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peter Augustus
                    Jay.</hi></signed></closer>




